    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Look at your fingertips. See those tiny swirly lines? Those are ridges.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/skin-normal",
        "text": "Tiny ridges",
        "cue": "ridges",
        "sub": "Swirly lines!",
        "sub_cue": "swirly"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "When did I get them?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Before you were born! They formed while you were growing inside your mum.",
      "punch": "born",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👶",
        "text": "Made before you were born",
        "cue": "born"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So why is mine different from yours?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Scientists think tiny pushes and bumps shaped your skin as it grew. So the ridges made a pattern all your own.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👆",
        "text": "A pattern all your own",
        "cue": "pattern",
        "sub": "Shaped by tiny pushes",
        "sub_cue": "pushes"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What about twins? They look exactly the same!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Even identical twins have different fingerprints! Their fingertips grew in their own way.",
      "punch": "twins",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👯",
        "text": "Twins? Still different!",
        "cue": "twins",
        "sub": "Each has their own",
        "sub_cue": "own"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Are there different kinds of fingerprints?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Three main shapes: loops, whorls and arches. With a grown-up, check yours with a magnifying glass!",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
